FA Cup holders Arsenal, as a [[Premier League]] club, entered the competition in the third round where they were drawn at home against fellow top-flight team Hull City in a repeat of [[2014 FA Cup final|the previous year's final]]. At the Emirates Stadium, [[Per Mertesacker]] scored in the 20th minute with a [[Header (association football)|header]] from an [[Alexis Sánchez]] [[Corner kick|corner]].  With eight minutes remaining, Sánchez doubled Arsenal's lead with a strike from inside the Hull [[penalty area]] and his side won the match 2&ndash;0.<ref>{{cite web |first=Jonathan |last=Jurejko |title=Arsenal 2–0 Hull City |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/30614334 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=4 January 2015 |access-date=18 April 2015 |archive-date=4 April 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150404203820/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/30614334 |url-status=live }}</ref> In the fourth round, Arsenal's opposition were [[EFL Championship|Championship]] team [[Brighton & Hove Albion F.C.|Brighton & Hove Albion]] away at the [[Falmer Stadium]].  Arsenal's Walcott opened the scoring after less than two minutes from a [[Calum Chambers]] [[Cross (association football)|cross]] before Özil made it 2&ndash;0 midway through the first half.  [[Chris O'Grady]] scored for Brighton five minutes after half-time but [[Tomáš Rosický]] restored Arsenal's two-goal advantage nine minutes later with a [[Volley (association football)|volley]] after a [[push and run|one-two]] with Giroud.  [[Sam Baldock]]'s 75th-minute goal made it 3&ndash;2 but no further goals were scored and Arsenal progressed to the fifth round.<ref>{{cite web |first=Saj |last=Chowdhury |title=Brighton & Hove Albion 2–3 Arsenal |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/30868916 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=25 January 2015 |access-date=18 April 2015 |archive-date=6 April 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150406074333/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/30868916 |url-status=live }}</ref>  There, they were drawn at home against [[Middlesbrough F.C.|Middlesbrough]], another Championship club, at the Emirates Stadium.  Giroud scored twice in the space of three first-half minutes and, after a goalless second half, Arsenal secured their passage to the sixth round with a 2–0 victory.<ref>{{cite web |first=Patrick |last=Jennings |title=Arsenal 2–0 Middlesbrough |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/31423103 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=15 February 2015 |access-date=18 April 2015 |archive-date=15 February 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150215150442/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/31423103 |url-status=live }}</ref>

Arsenal were drawn away at Manchester United in a match televised on [[BBC One]] on a Monday evening.  This led to criticism from [[Arsenal F.C. supporters|Arsenal supporters]] as they suggested there would be no trains back to London after the match.<ref>{{cite web |first=Tom |last=Sheen |title=Arsenal fans to pay just £20 to travel to FA Cup clash with Manchester United after club subsidise fares |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/premier-league/arsenal-fans-to-pay-just-20-to-travel-to-fa-cup-clash-with-manchester-united-after-club-subsidise-10059839.html |work=[[The Independent]] |date=18 February 2015 |access-date=18 April 2015 |archive-date=28 July 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200728000520/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/premier-league/arsenal-fans-to-pay-just-20-to-travel-to-fa-cup-clash-with-manchester-united-after-club-subsidise-10059839.html |url-status=live }}</ref>  Despite this, 9,000 away supporters attended the game at [[Old Trafford]].  [[Nacho Monreal]] gave the visiting side the lead in the 25th minute from close range after receiving a pass from [[Alex Oxlade-Chamberlain]].  [[Wayne Rooney]] equalised for Manchester United four minutes later, heading an [[Ángel Di María]] cross past [[Wojciech Szczęsny]] in the Arsenal goal.  Former Manchester United player Welbeck then capitalised on a poor backpass by [[Antonio Valencia]] to take possession of the ball, [[dribbling]] it round [[David de Gea]] and scoring to make it 2&ndash;1. Di María was [[sent off]] with 14 minutes of the game remaining and the match ended without further scoring.<ref>{{cite news |first=Jacob |last=Steinberg |title=Manchester United v Arsenal: FA Cup quarter-final |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2015/mar/09/manchester-united-v-arsenal-fa-cup-quarter-final-live |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=9 March 2015 |access-date=18 April 2015 |archive-date=18 April 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150418232826/http://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2015/mar/09/manchester-united-v-arsenal-fa-cup-quarter-final-live |url-status=live }}</ref> In the semi-finals at [[Wembley Stadium]], a [[neutral venue]], Arsenal faced Championship side [[Reading F.C.|Reading]]. Sánchez scored from close range in the 39th minute before Reading's [[Garath McCleary]] equalised with a volley nine minutes into the second half.  With the score level at the end of regular time, the match went into [[Overtime (sports)|extra time]] when Sánchez scored in [[stoppage time]] of the first period to restore his side's lead.  The second period of extra time was goalless ending the match 2&ndash;1, and Arsenal reached the FA Cup Final for the second consecutive year.<ref>{{cite web |title=Reading 1&ndash;2 Arsenal |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/32261616 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |first=Nabil |last=Hassan |date=18 April 2015 |access-date=18 April 2015 |archive-date=23 February 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160223113811/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/32261616 |url-status=live }}</ref>

