==Post-match==
[[File:Arsenal FA Cup Winners Parade (18351309601).jpg|thumb|Arsenal's Jack Wilshere was charged with misconduct by the FA for his role in their victory parade.]]
This was the sixth FA Cup win for manager [[Arsène Wenger]], putting him in joint first place for wins with [[George Ramsay (footballer, born 1855)|George Ramsay]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Arsene Wenger overtakes Sir Alex Ferguson to become FA Cup's joint most successful manager |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/sport/football/arsene-wenger-overtakes-sir-alex-ferguson-to-become-fa-cups-joint-most-successful-manager-10286294.html |work=[[Evening Standard]] |date=30 May 2015 |access-date=31 May 2015 |archive-date=3 June 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150603131553/http://www.standard.co.uk/sport/football/arsene-wenger-overtakes-sir-alex-ferguson-to-become-fa-cups-joint-most-successful-manager-10286294.html |url-status=live }}</ref>  Wenger said "We have shown today that we are a real team. I’d like to congratulate everyone, my players, my staff, the supporters" and described it as "the perfect day".<ref name=guardasit1/><ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/may/30/fa-cup-final-arsenal-aston-villa-alexis-sanchez | work = [[The Guardian]] | title = FA Cup final: Alexis Sánchez inspires Arsenal to win over Aston Villa | access-date = 7 June 2021 | date = 30 May 2015 | first = Daniel | last = Taylor | archive-date = 23 September 2017 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20170923180140/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/may/30/fa-cup-final-arsenal-aston-villa-alexis-sanchez | url-status = live }}</ref>  Mertesacker said "We deserved this today. We played on the front foot from the start and that makes a massive difference".<ref name=bbcasit>{{Cite news | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/32563518 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 7 June 2021 | title = FA Cup final as it happened | first1 = Tom | last1 = Rostance | first2 = Gary | last2 = Rose | archive-date = 25 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210525130828/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/32563518 | url-status = live }}</ref>  Sherwood conceded that Arsenal had deserved to win, saying "I can't make any excuses for that today, Arsenal were too good for us. We couldn't impose ourselves on them or nullify what they had."<ref name=bbcasit/>  His captain, Delph, agreed, noting "Arsenal showed why they deserved the win. We were up against it, we tried to dig deep but their quality shone through and we struggled."<ref name=bbcasit/>

The game was broadcast live in the UK on free-to-air TV on BBC One and on pay TV on [[BT Sport]]. It was the first FA Cup Final broadcast by the BBC in seven years and they restored the tradition of having an all-day build-up for the final, linking up with other BBC programmes.<ref name=beebcov/> The game's viewership on BBC One peaked at 8.8{{nbsp}}million with an average of 8{{nbsp}}million.<ref>{{cite web |first=John |last=Plunkett |title=BBC's FA Cup final coverage nets peak of nearly 9 million |url=https://www.theguardian.com/media/2015/jun/01/bbc-fa-cup-final-coverage-nets-peak-of-nearly-9-million |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=1 June 2015 |access-date=8 June 2015 |archive-date=8 June 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150608194122/http://www.theguardian.com/media/2015/jun/01/bbc-fa-cup-final-coverage-nets-peak-of-nearly-9-million |url-status=live }}</ref>

On Arsenal's victory parade after winning the final, [[Jack Wilshere]] led fans in a chant calling [[North London derby|local rivals]] [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]] "shit".<ref>{{cite web |first=Jacob |last=Steinberg |title=Jack Wilshere ticked off by Arsenal after foul-mouthed abuse of Spurs |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/may/31/arsenal-wilshere-anti-spurs-victory-parade |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=31 May 2015 |access-date=3 June 2015 |archive-date=2 June 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150602122729/http://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/may/31/arsenal-wilshere-anti-spurs-victory-parade |url-status=live }}</ref> Having previously been warned after a similar chant in the previous season's victory parade, The Football Association charged him with misconduct.<ref>{{cite web |title=Arsenal: Jack Wilshere charged with misconduct after parade |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/32994427 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=3 June 2015 |access-date=3 June 2015 |archive-date=4 June 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150604034853/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/32994427 |url-status=live }}</ref>  He admitted the charge, was fined £40,000 and was "severely warned as to his future conduct".<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.thefa.com/news/2015/jun/16/jack-wilshere-admits-charge-of-misconduct-170615 | date = 17 June 2015 | access-date = 14 July 2021 | title = Jack Wilshere has admitted an FA charge of misconduct | publisher = [[The Football Association]] | archive-date = 21 May 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210521015143/https://www.thefa.com/news/2015/jun/16/jack-wilshere-admits-charge-of-misconduct-170615 | url-status = live }}</ref>

Following a change in [[UEFA]] rules, this was the first season where runners-up in cup competitions did not enter the [[UEFA Europa League|Europa League]] if the winners had already qualified for Europe.<ref>{{Cite web |last=UEFA.com |date=2013-09-20 |title=Strategic talks in Dubrovnik |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0253-0d7eeaa71d98-7ddf54a81673-1000--strategic-talks-in-dubrovnik/ |access-date=2024-05-19 |website=[[UEFA]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=UEFA.com |date=2014-08-29 |title=New approach broadens Europa League appeal |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/news/0257-0def7f60e195-fd6dc0500321-1000--new-approach-broadens-europa-league-appeal/ |access-date=2024-05-19 |website=[[UEFA]] |language=en}}</ref> Therefore, as Arsenal had already qualified for the [[2015–16 UEFA Champions League|Champions League]] by finishing third in the Premier League, the remaining Europa League place went to [[Southampton F.C.|Southampton]], the highest-placed Premier League team that had not qualified for any European competition.<ref>{{cite web |first=Simon |last=Stone |title=Reading and Aston Villa need FA Cup win for Europa League spot |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/32358581 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=17 April 2015 |access-date=17 April 2015}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=Southampton claim Europa League spot |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/32948425 |access-date=2024-05-19 |work=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref>  As winners, Arsenal played Chelsea, winners of the Premier League, in the [[2015 FA Community Shield]] at Wembley.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/32856754|title=Arsenal 4 Aston Villa 0|date=30 May 2015|publisher=[[BBC Sport]]|access-date=3 June 2015}}</ref>

